s $\\overset{―}{AB}$ in the ratio $AT:TB=3:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OT}.$" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420465 1072 #uuid "6fe46ce7-a162-566e-a261-116569794a12" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420465 1074 "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAB,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-a+b \\\\  & =b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AT:TB=3:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AT}=\\frac{3}{8}\\overset{\\to }{AB}=\\frac{3}{8}(b-a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{3}{8}(b-a) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}a+\\frac{3}{8}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420466 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420464 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420466 1069 "q-77230" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420466 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420466 1071 "![](images/8c/8cf7d0520b1d0654d5749651595acd48b7a08f2b2d55142b18ca63b2ded20f55.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+2b$, find $\\lambda .$" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420466 1072 #uuid "b667d36f-710b-5326-b636-9597ec1ec3f2" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420466 1074 "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/9e/9edea1e3ad727d11d7bfac884f27c1b435233fa7df561dbe2a4f3af45ea16bfa.png)\n\nIn $△OBC$, we have:\n\n- $BC=3|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{BC}=3a.$ \n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}+\\overset{\\to }{BC} \\\\  & =2b+3a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=2b+\\lambda a=2b+3a.$ \n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =3\n$$" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420467 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420463 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420467 1069 "q-20413" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420467 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420467 1071 "![](images/4b/4bb7598c9ebae28be572508974cd025caa8f4a6c3313f025ff0f5ca55296334e.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $h=\\lambda f+\\mu g$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420467 1072 #uuid "d5f98ecb-0f26-50ae-9a82-cc334fd82c55" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420467 1074 "![](images/43/43642acdb991827b4e1e16744e8a69507a383a1319ae07efde78480af4bab166.png)\n\nIn $△OFH$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OF=2|g|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OF}$ and $g$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=2g.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $FH=3|f|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FH}$ has the opposite direction to $f$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{FH}=-3f.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FH} \\\\  & =2g-3f \\\\  & =-3f+2g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $h=\\lambda f+\\mu g=-3f+2g.$\n\nSince $f∦g,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420468 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420469 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420468 1062 #uuid "509e4633-305b-52c6-89d7-db63ec41fd87" 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420468 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420467 13194139534385 17592186045417 true] [17592186420469 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420470 13194139534385 175